    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "About two hundred years ago, people found Antarctica. It is an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "amazing",
            "zh": "令人惊叹的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " place!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Antarctica is the coldest continent of all. It also has the strongest winds, and the lowest rainfall and snowfall."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Most of the fresh water on Earth is frozen in Antarctica’s ice. The ice has "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "built up",
            "zh": "累积"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " over many thousands of years. That is because the snow doesn’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "melt",
            "ref": "v-melt"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "completely",
            "zh": "彻底地"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the cold summers there."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Antarctica is a dangerous place to live. No trees grow on the continent. Only low plants, like "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "moss",
            "zh": "苔藓"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", grow there. Most plants and animals can be found near the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "coasts",
            "ref": "v-coast"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or in the sea."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Antarctica is a “playground” for scientists. Some of them work there all year round. Others work there only in the summer. They study animals, ice and many other things."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "在南极，科学家们利用钻孔机，让钻头穿过冰盖最上层，钻入下面的古代冻结层。在那里，被困住的微小气泡充当了已逝环境的“时间胶囊”。钻取出的冰芯使科学家得以研究过往的气候变化。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
